        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A mixture of Al(OiPr)3 (204 mg, 1 mmol), CAN (46 mg, 0.083 mmol), cerium(III) nitrate hexahydrate (145 mg, 0.33 mmol), 3-aminobenzoic acid (137 mg, 1 mmol), pyridine (0.2 mL), and MeCN (5 mL) was sealed in a 20 mL vial and heated at 80 °C for 5 days. After cooling to room temperature and standing for 1 day, prismatic purple crystals of AlOC-129Ce were obtained. Crystals were rinsed with Py/MeCN (1:25, v/v) and stored sealed and dry.",
